description:
Build `IntList`, a singly linked list whose nodes are owned by `std::unique_ptr`, with a raw pointer to the last node so that `push_back` is O(1):

```cpp
class IntList
{
public:
    void push_front(int value);
    void push_back(int value);
    int pop_front();                       // returns the value; std::out_of_range if empty
    std::size_t size() const;
    bool empty() const;
    std::vector<int> toVector() const;
    void reverse();                        // in place, O(n), no new nodes
    std::size_t removeAll(int value);      // removes every node holding value; returns how many
    bool hasValue(int value) const;
    int middle() const;                    // the middle value (the second of the two middles for an even size); std::out_of_range if empty
    ~IntList();                            // must not recurse once per node
};
```

Keep `tail_` correct after **every** operation, including `reverse` and `removeAll` (the tests push to the back afterwards). `middle` uses the fast and slow pointers from lesson 1.04.

